## STEP 2 — COMPOSE A SOUL (brand register only) — don't pick one off a list

Soul diversity is the job. **A closed list of personas yields one page per row** — a model choosing from a menu lands on the same two or three every time, weighted by what it has seen most. So **draw one value per axis and let the combination be the soul.** Five axes with a handful of values each is thousands of combinations, not ten.

| Axis | Values (extend freely) |
|---|---|
| **A · Palette** | mono + one acid pop · dual-hue conflict · monochrome by opacity ladder only · earth + one saturated · near-black + dual metal · light ground + ink + one signal |
| **B · Type** | display and body from one superfamily · extreme weight contrast (900 vs 300) · serif italic *inside* a sans headline as the only human note · mono-forward · one variable font in every role · display so large it *is* the layout |
| **C · Layout family** | hover-expand accordion · pinned horizontal track · generative (algorithmically split) grid · table/list rows instead of cards · geometric collage · asymmetric weighted grid · exploded-view diagram · full-bleed photographic stack · pinned panel stepper |
| **D · Engine** | Three.js structure · Canvas 2D field · WebGL FBO (fluid / reaction-diffusion) · GSAP scrub choreography · CSS-only geometry · variable-font morph · **no engine — typography carries it** |
| **E · Material** | film & contact sheet · paper & press · machined metal · water & fluid · signal & phosphor · laboratory & specimen · textile & thread · concrete & light · circuitry & grid |

**Draw on E first** — the material is where the page's *reason* lives, and it honestly constrains the other four.

These are known-good combinations, for calibration only — **cinematic tech** (cool dual-hue + sans/mono + Three.js + circuitry), **phosphor terminal** (mono+acid + mono-forward + Canvas + signal), **editorial** (cream/ink + serif pair + GSAP + paper), **brutal typographic** (bone/black+hot + display-as-layout + press), **quiet luxury** (off-white/sage + one family 100–900 + CSS-only + concrete).

**Break ties with a die, not with willpower.** When two directions are equally defensible, you will silently take the one you've seen most — that's the whole disease. Roll (`date +%S`, mod the axis length), and **if you override the roll, write down why.**

Rules: **one soul per page**, never fluctuate. Saturated defaults (AI-purple-glow, beige+brass) are banned unless earned. **An *observed* brand fact always beats a ban list and a die roll** — the bans exist to stop *you* defaulting, never to overrule a real brand.

