## STEP 7 — PERFORMANCE & A11Y

**The motion gate — read the two probes once, then branch per effect.** ("Support reduced-motion" as an abstract instruction is why most pages ship it broken.)

```js
const REDUCE = matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
const FINE   = matchMedia('(hover:hover) and (pointer:fine)').matches;
```

- **`REDUCE`** gates everything that *moves*; **`FINE`** gates everything that depends on a *pointer* (magnetic buttons, cursor followers, hover-expand, tilt) so it never fires on touch.
- **Every animation ships its terminal state.** The branch is **not** `if (!REDUCE) animate()` — that leaves the element at its *initial* (usually `opacity: 0`) state. **A reveal gated off with no terminal state is an invisible page, not a calm one.** Do: `if (REDUCE) el.classList.add('is-visible'); else gsap.to(el, {...})`.
- **Canvas loops must actually stop** — put the guard *inside* the loop, never rely on `cancelAnimationFrame` ordering:
  ```js
  function frame() { draw(t); if (!REDUCE) { t += .016; raf = requestAnimationFrame(frame); } }
  frame();   // reduced-motion → one composed still, then stops
  ```
  The still must be **composed, not empty** — pick a `t` where the visual reads as designed (`t = 0` is often the degenerate flat state).
- **Un-pin, don't un-animate.** A pinned section with its animation disabled traps the scroll forever. Under `REDUCE`, set `position: static` and let the panels stack.
- CSS backstop, always paired: `@media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){*{animation-duration:.001ms!important;transition-duration:.001ms!important}}`
- **Verify by forcing reduced-motion on and looking**: every section visible, composed, readable. Anything blank is a bug.

**Canvas is blurry on retina unless you say otherwise:** `DPR = Math.min(2, devicePixelRatio||1)`; `canvas.width = W*DPR` (buffer) while `canvas.style.width = W+'px'` (CSS box) — then multiply **every** drawing constant by `DPR`.

- Animate `transform`/`opacity` only. `will-change` sparingly.
- WCAG AA: body ≥ 4.5:1, large text ≥ 3:1 — **on the actual photo, in the actual crop**, not against the average color.
- Visible focus states on every interactive element.
- Lazy-load heavy engines. `min-h-dvh` over `100vh`. CLS < 0.1.
- Touch targets ≥ 44px. Mobile layout declared per multi-column section. **Hiding the nav links on mobile with no replacement is a bug, not responsive design.**

---

## STEP 8 — PRE-FLIGHT (mandatory before "done")

Check all of:
- [ ] Design Read output with committed register + dials
- [ ] Premium substrate applied (grain, vignette, type tension, translucent borders, color lock)
- [ ] SPECTACLE claimed = SPECTACLE shipped (working engine if ≥7) — verify in a browser if available: open the page, confirm the hero renders real pixels, not a white/flat screen
- [ ] Cheapness blacklist cleared (em-dashes, gradient text, eyebrow spam, fake numbers)
- [ ] `prefers-reduced-motion` handled
- [ ] WCAG AA contrast verified
- [ ] Layout families diversified — no repeated pattern dominance
- [ ] Mobile layout declared

If any hard rule fails, fix before delivery. Shipping broken work is not an option.
